   "source": [
    "## Part 1 — Problem Definition and Data Collection\n",
    "\n",
    "Three Sydney suburbs were chosen to represent distinct housing markets:\n",
    "- **Mosman** — harbourside, high-income, heritage/prestige housing (~9 km from CBD)\n",
    "- **Marrickville** — inner-west, gentrifying, mixed Victorian/Federation cottages and apartments (~7 km from CBD)\n",
    "- **Blacktown** — outer-western Sydney, family-oriented, larger/more affordable housing (~30+ km from CBD)\n",
    "\n",
    "These differ substantially in price, dwelling mix, and distance-to-CBD, giving a harder and more realistic\n",
    "generalisation test than three similar suburbs would.\n"
   ]
  },
