   "source": [
    "def metrics(actual, pred):\n",
    "    err = pred-actual\n",
    "    return np.abs(err).mean(), (err**2).mean()**0.5, (np.abs(err)/actual).mean()*100, np.corrcoef(actual, pred)[0,1]\n",
    "\n",
    "rows=[]\n",
    "for label,col in [('ML Model (Ridge)','ML_Pred'), ('LLM (Claude)','LLM_Pred'), ('Human-style CMA heuristic','HumanEst')]:\n",
    "    mae,rmse,mape,corr = metrics(sel['SalePrice'], sel[col])\n",
    "    rows.append({'Approach':label,'MAE ($)':mae,'RMSE ($)':rmse,'MAPE (%)':mape,'Correlation (r)':corr})\n",
    "pd.DataFrame(rows).round(3)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3b863294",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "On this small sample the CMA heuristic achieved the lowest overall error (MAPE ≈9.5%), narrowly ahead of the\n",
    "ML model (≈10.5%), with the LLM valuation trailing (≈12.9%) — though all three correlated strongly with actual\n",
    "prices (r>0.99). A simple suburb-specific $/sqm rate is a strong baseline precisely because location and building\n",
    "size dominate price here. Human/local-comparable knowledge still adds value, especially at the edges of the\n",
    "training distribution where ML and general LLM knowledge are weakest."
   ]
  },
