   "source": [
    "### Critical reflection\n",
    "\n",
    "The most important lesson from this project was methodological: the biggest threat to a valid property-valuation\n",
    "pipeline is data provenance and sample size, not model choice. With genuinely collected, larger data, the tree\n",
    "ensembles would likely overtake Ridge. Feature engineering was the most defensible stage — building area,\n",
    "location, and room counts dominated as hypothesised, and the NLP luxury-score feature added genuine signal.\n",
    "Ethically, a model trained on a narrow set of suburbs will extrapolate poorly and silently outside its training\n",
    "distribution, and should be paired with confidence flags and human review for atypical properties rather than\n",
    "presented as an authoritative point estimate. See the PDF report for the full discussion."
   ]
  }
